<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for BookMe: Guided Book Writer." />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#17120d" />
  <title>BookMe — Privacy Policy</title>

  <style>
    :root {
      --ink: #2a2118;
      --ink-soft: #5e4b36;
      --parchment: #f3e4be;
      --parchment-2: #e7cf98;
      --gold: #d7a84c;
      --gold-soft: #f0cf7d;
      --moon: #d9c7ff;
      --amethyst: #7257a8;
      --amethyst-soft: #a989d8;
      --emerald: #2f5f50;
      --teal-magic: #3e7b74;
      --night: #0d0b12;
      --night-2: #17111f;
      --wine: #6e304d;
      --forest: #2d5647;
      --line: rgba(74, 52, 28, 0.22);
      --shadow: 0 24px 65px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.42);
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      background: var(--night);
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      line-height: 1.72;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 18% 10%, rgba(215,168,76,.18), transparent 28%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 82% 18%, rgba(114,87,168,.22), transparent 30%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 72%, rgba(62,123,116,.13), transparent 34%),
        linear-gradient(160deg, var(--night), var(--night-2) 52%, #09080d);
      min-height: 100vh;
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }

    .stars,
    .stars::before,
    .stars::after {
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      content: "";
      z-index: 0;
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(circle, rgba(240,207,125,.85) 0 1px, transparent 1.6px),
        radial-gradient(circle, rgba(217,199,255,.62) 0 1px, transparent 1.5px),
        radial-gradient(circle, rgba(169,137,216,.45) 0 1px, transparent 1.4px);
      background-size: 92px 92px, 143px 143px, 211px 211px;
      background-position: 0 0, 37px 71px, 83px 24px;
      opacity: .24;
      animation: drift 24s linear infinite;
    }

    .stars::before {
      transform: scale(1.2);
      opacity: .12;
      animation-duration: 34s;
    }

    .stars::after {
      transform: scale(.8);
      opacity: .1;
      animation-duration: 42s;
    }

    @keyframes drift {
      from { transform: translateY(0); }
      to   { transform: translateY(-92px); }
    }

    .shell {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      width: min(100% - 28px, 980px);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 54px 0 70px;
    }

    .crest-wrap {
      position: relative;
      width: 132px;
      height: 116px;
      margin: 0 auto 6px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
    }

    .crest {
      width: 74px;
      height: 74px;
      margin: 0;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      border: 1px solid rgba(229,199,125,.55);
      border-radius: 50%;
      color: var(--gold-soft);
      font-size: 36px;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, rgba(114,87,168,.34), transparent 42%),
        rgba(13,11,18,.78);
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 8px rgba(215,168,76,.05),
        0 0 34px rgba(215,168,76,.20),
        0 0 62px rgba(114,87,168,.18);
      animation: glow 4s ease-in-out infinite;
      position: relative;
      z-index: 2;
    }

    .sparkle {
      position: absolute;
      z-index: 1;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1;
      opacity: .82;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 0 7px currentColor);
      animation: twinkle 2.6s ease-in-out infinite;
      user-select: none;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .sparkle.s1 { left: 10px; top: 25px; color: #d9c7ff; animation-delay: .1s; }
    .sparkle.s2 { right: 9px; top: 18px; color: #f0cf7d; animation-delay: .7s; }
    .sparkle.s3 { left: 24px; bottom: 16px; color: #67b6a3; animation-delay: 1.15s; }
    .sparkle.s4 { right: 24px; bottom: 11px; color: #b690e8; animation-delay: 1.65s; }
    .sparkle.s5 { left: 3px; top: 57px; color: #e9a0c3; animation-delay: 2s; font-size: 10px; }
    .sparkle.s6 { right: 3px; top: 55px; color: #8fd4c4; animation-delay: 2.3s; font-size: 10px; }

    @keyframes twinkle {
      0%, 100% {
        transform: scale(.75) rotate(0deg);
        opacity: .35;
      }
      50% {
        transform: scale(1.18) rotate(18deg);
        opacity: 1;
      }
    }

    @keyframes glow {
      0%, 100% {
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px rgba(215,168,76,.05), 0 0 30px rgba(215,168,76,.15), 0 0 50px rgba(114,87,168,.10);
      }
      50% {
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 11px rgba(215,168,76,.07), 0 0 48px rgba(215,168,76,.26), 0 0 72px rgba(114,87,168,.22);
      }
    }

    .hero {
      text-align: center;
      color: #f8efd8;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      letter-spacing: .18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--gold-soft);
      font-size: .78rem;
      margin-bottom: 7px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
      line-height: 1;
      margin: 0;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -.035em;
      text-shadow:
        0 2px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.45),
        0 0 28px rgba(114,87,168,.18);
    }

    .subtitle {
      max-width: 690px;
      margin: 16px auto 0;
      color: rgba(246,236,210,.74);
      font-size: 1.03rem;
    }

    .quick-nav {
      display: flex;
      gap: 9px;
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin: 23px auto 32px;
    }

    .quick-nav a {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      color: #fff3cf;
      text-decoration: none;
      padding: 9px 14px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(236,207,139,.42);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background:
        linear-gradient(110deg,
          rgba(103,74,142,.34),
          rgba(44,98,83,.28) 48%,
          rgba(167,112,61,.28));
      box-shadow:
        inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.12),
        inset 0 0 18px rgba(114,87,168,.06),
        0 0 12px rgba(114,87,168,.07);
      transition:
        transform .18s ease,
        background .22s ease,
        border-color .18s ease,
        box-shadow .22s ease;
      font-size: .9rem;
      backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
    }

    .quick-nav a::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: -40% -70%;
      background: linear-gradient(
        115deg,
        transparent 38%,
        rgba(255,255,255,.20) 49%,
        transparent 60%
      );
      transform: translateX(-45%) rotate(3deg);
      transition: transform .55s ease;
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .quick-nav a:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.015);
      background:
        linear-gradient(110deg,
          rgba(123,91,169,.48),
          rgba(49,118,98,.40) 48%,
          rgba(194,139,74,.40));
      border-color: rgba(240,207,125,.72);
      box-shadow:
        0 0 16px rgba(114,87,168,.16),
        0 0 24px rgba(62,123,116,.08),
        inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.16);
    }

    .quick-nav a:hover::after {
      transform: translateX(55%) rotate(3deg);
    }

    .scroll {
      position: relative;
      border: 1px solid rgba(105,75,39,.44);
      border-radius: 20px;
      padding: clamp(25px, 5vw, 58px);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 10% 8%, rgba(114,87,168,.075), transparent 19%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 92% 90%, rgba(62,123,116,.07), transparent 22%),
        linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,.15), rgba(255,255,255,.025)),
        repeating-linear-gradient(
          0deg,
          rgba(105,75,39,.024) 0,
          rgba(105,75,39,.024) 1px,
          transparent 1px,
          transparent 5px
        ),
        linear-gradient(135deg, var(--parchment), #f9efd4 47%, var(--parchment-2));
      box-shadow:
        var(--shadow),
        0 0 0 1px rgba(240,207,125,.06),
        0 0 80px rgba(114,87,168,.10);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .scroll::before,
    .scroll::after {
      content: "✦";
      position: absolute;
      color: rgba(106,76,36,.23);
      font-size: 58px;
      line-height: 1;
    }

    .scroll::before { top: 16px; left: 19px; }
    .scroll::after  { right: 19px; bottom: 14px; transform: rotate(45deg); }

    .seal {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 9px;
      padding: 7px 11px;
      border-radius: 8px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(108,47,53,.24);
      background:
        linear-gradient(90deg,
          rgba(108,47,83,.08),
          rgba(114,87,168,.08),
          rgba(47,95,80,.08));
      color: #5a2f43;
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 18px rgba(114,87,168,.035);
      font-size: .88rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }

    section {
      scroll-margin-top: 22px;
      padding: 8px 0 27px;
      margin-bottom: 17px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    section:last-of-type {
      border-bottom: 0;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    h2 {
      position: relative;
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      color: #332516;
      font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
      line-height: 1.24;
    }

    h2::after {
      content: "";
      display: block;
      width: 82px;
      height: 2px;
      margin-top: 8px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(114,87,168,.68),
        rgba(62,123,116,.62),
        rgba(215,168,76,.72)
      );
      box-shadow: 0 0 9px rgba(114,87,168,.12);
    }

    h2::before {
      content: "✧";
      color: #7a5e9f;
      text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(114,87,168,.22);
      margin-right: 9px;
      font-size: .85em;
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 18px 0 7px;
      color: #4b3721;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    p { margin: 0 0 12px; }

    ul {
      margin: 8px 0 14px;
      padding-left: 24px;
    }

    li { margin: 6px 0; }

    a {
      color: #6b3d1f;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .callout {
      margin: 16px 0;
      padding: 16px 17px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(40,72,60,.24);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--forest);
      border-radius: 11px;
      background:
        linear-gradient(100deg,
          rgba(40,72,60,.075),
          rgba(114,87,168,.045),
          rgba(200,157,69,.055));
    }

    .subscription-card {
      margin: 16px 0;
      padding: 18px;
      border-radius: 14px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(106,76,36,.22);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.25);
      box-shadow: inset 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.4);
    }

    .subscription-card strong {
      color: #50351c;
    }

    .small {
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-size: .94rem;
    }

    .footer {
      text-align: center;
      color: rgba(246,236,210,.68);
      margin-top: 28px;
      font-size: .88rem;
      text-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(114,87,168,.10);
    }

    .footer a { color: var(--gold-soft); }

    .top-link {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 7px;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .placeholder {
      background: rgba(151,84,48,.10);
      border-bottom: 1px dashed rgba(108,47,53,.62);
      padding: 0 3px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #6a2d33;
    }

    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .shell { padding-top: 34px; }
      .scroll { border-radius: 15px; }
      .quick-nav { margin-bottom: 23px; }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *, *::before, *::after {
        animation: none !important;
        scroll-behavior: auto !important;
        transition: none !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body id="top">
  <div class="stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <main class="shell">
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="crest-wrap" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="sparkle s1">✦</span>
        <span class="sparkle s2">✧</span>
        <span class="sparkle s3">✦</span>
        <span class="sparkle s4">✧</span>
        <span class="sparkle s5">✦</span>
        <span class="sparkle s6">✧</span>
        <div class="crest">🔐</div>
      </div>
      <div class="eyebrow">The BookMe Codex</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        A clear account of how BookMe handles your information — designed to protect
        the stories, ideas, and creative work entrusted to the app.
      </p>
      <div aria-hidden="true" style="
        margin:18px auto 0;
        color:#d9c7ff;
        letter-spacing:.34em;
        font-size:.92rem;
        text-shadow:0 0 18px rgba(169,137,216,.45);
      ">✦ ✧ ☾ ✧ ✦</div>
    </header>

    <nav class="quick-nav" aria-label="Privacy navigation">
      <a href="#collect">What We Collect</a>
      <a href="#use">How We Use It</a>
      <a href="#ai">AI Features</a>
      <a href="#sharing">Sharing</a>
      <a href="#retention">Retention</a>
      <a href="#rights">Your Rights</a>
      <a href="#children">Children</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="scroll">
      <div class="seal">✦ Effective September 10, 2026</div>

      <section id="overview">
        <h2>1. Privacy at a Glance</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>BookMe: Guided Book Writer</strong>
          (“BookMe,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, stores, shares, and protects
          information when you use the BookMe application and related services.
        </p>
        <p>
          BookMe is a guided writing application that may include account features,
          manuscript and note storage, profile and community features, image uploads,
          AI-assisted writing tools, subscriptions, and related app functionality.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Short version:</strong> we use information to operate BookMe,
          save and sync your work, provide the features you request, maintain account
          security, process subscription access, support community features, and improve
          reliability. We do not sell your personal information.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="collect">
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Account and Contact Information</h3>
        <p>
          When you create or use an account, we may collect information such as your
          <strong>email address, display name, profile information, and internal user identifier</strong>.
        </p>

        <h3>Your Writing and Other User Content</h3>
        <p>
          We may collect and store content you intentionally create, upload, or submit,
          including manuscripts, chapters, notes, outlines, prompts, titles, book details,
          profile text, comments or reactions, and other written material.
        </p>

        <h3>Photos and Images</h3>
        <p>
          If you choose to upload images, BookMe may collect profile pictures, book-cover
          images, manuscript images, or other images you submit through the app.
        </p>

        <h3>Subscription and Purchase Information</h3>
        <p>
          If you purchase a subscription through the Apple App Store, Apple processes the
          payment. BookMe may receive information needed to determine your subscription
          status, product entitlement, renewal state, or purchase validation. We do
          <strong>not</strong> receive your full credit-card or bank-account details from Apple.
        </p>

        <h3>Usage and Diagnostic Information</h3>
        <p>
          BookMe may collect limited technical information needed to operate and improve
          the service, such as app interactions, device or app identifiers, crash reports,
          diagnostic information, performance information, and error logs, if those
          services are enabled in the version of BookMe you use.
        </p>

        <h3>Information You Choose to Make Public</h3>
        <p>
          If you use community or sharing features, information you intentionally publish
          may be visible to other BookMe users. This may include a display name, profile
          image, book information, writing excerpts, reactions, progress information, or
          other content you choose to share.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="use">
        <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>We may use collected information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>create, authenticate, and maintain your account;</li>
          <li>save, sync, organize, display, and export your writing and other content;</li>
          <li>provide writing, planning, editing, community, and personalization features;</li>
          <li>provide and verify subscription or premium-feature access;</li>
          <li>process requests you make through AI-assisted writing tools;</li>
          <li>moderate uploaded content and help protect users from abuse or prohibited material;</li>
          <li>provide customer support and respond to questions;</li>
          <li>detect fraud, abuse, security incidents, and technical problems;</li>
          <li>maintain, troubleshoot, and improve BookMe; and</li>
          <li>comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="ai">
        <h2>4. AI-Assisted Writing Features</h2>
        <p>
          BookMe may offer optional AI-assisted features such as brainstorming,
          rewriting, polishing, expanding, shortening, summarizing, grammar assistance,
          contextual suggestions, or other writing help.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you intentionally use an AI feature, the text, prompt, selected passage,
          contextual writing, or other information necessary to respond to your request
          may be sent to an AI service provider for processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use AI-related information only as reasonably necessary to provide the
          feature you requested, maintain safety and reliability, and operate the service,
          subject to the practices of the applicable service provider.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          BookMe does not require you to use AI tools in order to write. Avoid submitting
          information to AI features that you do not want processed as part of an AI request.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing">
        <h2>5. When Information May Be Shared</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information. We may share information only in
          circumstances such as the following:
        </p>

        <h3>Service Providers</h3>
        <p>
          We may use trusted providers for services such as cloud hosting and databases,
          authentication, file storage, subscription management, AI processing, email
          delivery, analytics, crash reporting, security, or other infrastructure needed
          to operate BookMe. They may process information on our behalf to provide those services.
        </p>

        <h3>Community Features</h3>
        <p>
          Content you intentionally publish through community features may be shared with
          and visible to other users according to the settings and features you choose.
          Drafts and private writing are not made public merely because they are stored in BookMe.
        </p>

        <h3>Legal and Safety Reasons</h3>
        <p>
          We may disclose information when reasonably necessary to comply with law,
          respond to valid legal process, enforce our Terms, investigate fraud or abuse,
          protect the security of BookMe, or protect the rights and safety of users or others.
        </p>

        <h3>Business Changes</h3>
        <p>
          If BookMe is involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization,
          bankruptcy, or sale of assets, information may be transferred as part of that
          transaction, subject to applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="tracking">
        <h2>6. Advertising and Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          BookMe is not designed around third-party behavioral advertising. We do not
          sell your personal information for advertising purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          If BookMe later introduces advertising, cross-app tracking, or materially
          different data practices, this Privacy Policy and applicable App Store privacy
          disclosures will be updated before those practices are used where required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="moderation">
        <h2>7. Community Safety and Moderation</h2>
        <p>
          BookMe may process user-generated content and related account information to
          operate reporting, blocking, moderation, abuse prevention, image moderation,
          and other community-safety functions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Content reported by users or detected by safety systems may be reviewed and,
          when appropriate, restricted or removed in accordance with our Terms of Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention">
        <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide BookMe,
          maintain your account, fulfill the purposes described in this Policy, comply
          with legal obligations, resolve disputes, enforce agreements, and maintain
          security and fraud-prevention records.
        </p>
        <p>
          Retention periods may differ depending on the type of information. Some backup,
          transaction, security, or legal records may remain for a limited period after
          account or content deletion where permitted or required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security">
        <h2>9. Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards
          intended to protect information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse,
          alteration, or disclosure. No internet-connected service can guarantee absolute
          security, so users should also protect their login credentials and devices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights">
        <h2>10. Your Choices and Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to,
          correction of, deletion of, or a copy of certain personal information, or to
          object to or restrict certain processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also remove or edit certain information directly through BookMe where
          those controls are provided. For privacy or deletion requests, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:lecoffeeconfit@gmail.com">lecoffeeconfit@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may need to verify your identity before fulfilling certain requests.
          We will respond in accordance with applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="california">
        <h2>11. California Privacy Notice</h2>
        <p>
          California residents may have additional privacy rights under applicable
          California law. Depending on whether a particular law applies to BookMe,
          those rights may include requesting information about categories of personal
          information collected, requesting deletion or correction, and exercising
          other applicable privacy choices.
        </p>
        <p>
          BookMe does not sell personal information. To make a California privacy
          request, email
          <a href="mailto:lecoffeeconfit@gmail.com">lecoffeeconfit@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <h2>12. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          BookMe is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
          personal information from children under 13 in violation of applicable law.
          If you believe a child has provided personal information improperly, contact
          us so we can investigate and take appropriate action.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="international">
        <h2>13. Data Processing Locations</h2>
        <p>
          BookMe and its service providers may process information in the United States
          and other locations where they operate. Privacy protections and laws may differ
          between jurisdictions. Where required, we use appropriate measures for
          international data transfers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="third-party">
        <h2>14. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
        <p>
          BookMe may rely on third-party platforms or services to provide infrastructure,
          subscriptions, authentication, AI processing, or other functionality. Their
          handling of information may also be governed by their own privacy policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          BookMe may also contain links to third-party sites. We are not responsible for
          the privacy practices of websites or services that we do not control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to
          BookMe, our data practices, legal requirements, or service providers. When
          appropriate, we may provide notice through the app, our website, email, or
